  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Enhancement for institutionalized victim centered investigations and prosecutions of Trafficking in Persons (TIP) Cases</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM) will build the criminal justice process around a victim-centered approach by enhancing cooperation and coordination among members of the national TIP task forces. Project activities will include increasing the capacity of TIP knowledge among already established anti-TIP task forces to better identify TIP cases, revising and mainstreaming a counter trafficking curriculum into the training programs of targeted government departments, and developing and strengthening TIP data collection and reporting mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
